<h2>Indian dried red chilli for export</h2>
<p>Red chilli is India's single largest spice export by value, and Andhra Pradesh — with Guntur as the country's principal chilli trading hub — is the backbone of that trade, alongside Telangana and Karnataka. We supply whole pods (with or without stem) and crushed/ground chilli across the main commercial varieties, matched to whether a buyer needs heat, colour, or both.</p>

<p>Harvest runs January-April depending on region and variety. Pods are sun-dried after picking, then cleaned and graded; well-dried chilli stores for many months, which is why we can supply from stock through the year rather than only immediately after harvest.</p>

<h2>How should I specify red chilli?</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Variety.</strong> Teja for high pungency, Byadgi for deep colour with milder heat, Sannam and other regional types in between. Your end use — direct food heat, colour extraction, or both — should drive the choice.</li>
  <li><strong>Form.</strong> Whole pods keep longer and travel better; stemless whole pods suit buyers who want to skip that step; crushed/ground is ready for direct use but shorter-lived.</li>
  <li><strong>Pungency and colour.</strong> Scoville Heat Units and ASTA colour value both vary by variety and season — we confirm both on the certificate of analysis rather than presenting a single number as fixed across all lots.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Which markets buy Indian red chilli?</h2>
<p>China is by a clear margin the largest single market, feeding food-processing and oleoresin-extraction demand at scale, followed by Thailand, the United States, Bangladesh and Sri Lanka — see the cited table below for the full country breakdown.</p>
<p>Shipping specifically to <a href="/products/spices/red-chilli/china/">China</a>, <a href="/products/spices/red-chilli/usa/">the USA</a> or <a href="/products/spices/red-chilli/bangladesh/">Bangladesh</a>? Each has its own dedicated route page covering the specific registration, testing and documentation requirements for that market.</p>

<h2>Red chilli export pricing</h2>
<p>Chilli pricing moves with variety, pungency grade, form and current-season crop conditions in Andhra Pradesh and Telangana. Send your variety, form, quantity and destination port and we'll quote current FOB/CIF terms.</p>

